# Epic: Historical PFP Audit and Residual Preflight Remediation

**Epic ID:** `EPIC-OE-PFP-000`
**AuthorityEffect:** None
**Status:** `LIVE`

**Lifecycle scope:** LIVE — residual remediation
**Date:** October 2026
**Target Subsystems:** `education/pfp`, `symbol_game`

## Historical source and current review basis

The [audit review](../../../../_docs/audits/pfp_pilots_2026-10-10/review.md) and [per-entry inventory](../../../../_docs/audits/pfp_pilots_2026-10-10/inventory.md) describe 338 registered/related entries and 1,260 Python files at `df84a596`. Its 39 focused tests and nine probes are historical scoped claims. The leakage, coercion and cache findings refer to that snapshot; they must not be presented as unchanged current behavior.

Current [live_evaluator.py](../../../../education/pilots/live_evaluator.py) separates request construction from private expected answers, uses the strict registered checker and validates bound v2 observations. [checker_registry.py](../../../../education/pfp/domain/pilots/checker_registry.py) refuses duplicate keys and malformed types. [pilot_evidence.py](../../../../education/pfp/infrastructure/pilot_evidence.py) binds request/spec/seed/checker bytes and writes immutable evaluation records. These are implementation facts, not proof that every historical seed/family is clean or every campaign gate is complete.

The live evaluator still dispatches directly rather than through the planned durable common reservation/confinement service. Its evidence remains `efficacy_eligible=False`; missing cost remains unknown. Historical regrading does not become clean-campaign efficacy evidence.

## Residual remediation workstreams

| Historical vector | Current bounded obligation |
|---|---|
| F01 answer leakage / F04 stored answers | Test private oracle-only sentinels against actual dispatch bytes. Inventory legacy seed/checker bindings separately; public task numerals remain valid inputs. |
| F02 permissive grading | Exercise actual strict parsing/type/refusal branches, not permissive historical examples. Bind each finite checker to a reviewed independent oracle. |
| F03/F09 accounting | Implement PFP-002 durable reservations, unresolved-attempt handling, reconciled usage and common confinement before campaign qualification. |
| F05 cache custody | Reject altered/transplanted request, observation, spec, seed and checker bindings; preserve append-only original evaluations and recovery. |
| F06 helper duplication | Extract only a demonstrated shared helper after a real consumer needs it; preserve independent judges rather than merging them to obtain agreement. |
| F07 replay routes | Inventory actual missing catalogs/imports/registered targets before adding any route; retired migration routes are not automatically restored. |
| F08 synthetic pass rows | Require real checker execution and scoped immutable evidence; static flags and self-authored PASS are insufficient. |
| F10 experiment design | Separate one-call check permutations from independently dispatched model repetitions. |

## Dependencies, acceptance and ceiling

PFP-001 supplies typed ingress; PFP-002 supplies durable service/reservation semantics; PFP-003 verifies the first integrated finite slice. Begin with one private-oracle request and one malformed/transplanted observation, then expand only after the independent witness and mutation recovery are retained.

No all-75-config, all-26-seed or whole-estate remediation is claimed by source inspection alone. Scaling to 2,500 scenarios remains conditional on scoped preflight receipts and complete campaign provenance. This plan runs no live model trial and grants no release authority.

## Obstruction review and TDD test plan

**Review basis (2026-10-10):** The df84a596 audit and its39-test report are historical. Current [live_evaluator.py](../../../../education/pilots/live_evaluator.py) already uses strict checker registration, builds response schemas without an expected-answer argument, refuses historical response reuse and records immutable observations. [pilot_evidence.py](../../../../education/pfp/infrastructure/pilot_evidence.py) already binds spec/seed/request/checker digests. Reproduce any remaining defect at the selected head before repair; F01–F10 below are snapshot findings, not current reproductions. Dispatch still uses urllib directly, so shared budget confinement remains an integration obligation.

**Bounded behavior and public port:** Existing `build_live_request`, `extract_and_evaluate`, `run_live_evaluator` over a temporary one-pilot tree; `write_once`/`record_evaluation` are the custody seam. A local recording transport receives public task bytes only. Use a private oracle-only sentinel: a number legitimately present in the public task is not answer leakage.

**Dependencies and review routing:** Implement one case at a time after the stated dependency is available. Syntax Prefilter checks malformed input; Bare Metal Anchor/Techne implements the smallest production change; Defect Hunter and the Inspector challenge the independent oracle; Punchlist checks custody before Adversary records the scoped result. Use the four stages intake, implementation, adversarial QA, and receipt review. Stop after at most three repair attempts and retain the blocking witness.

| Order | One-test RED → minimal GREEN → refactor slice | Proposed test and oracle |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | RED when an oracle-only sentinel enters request bytes; remove only the answer-bearing source field, then refactor builder validation. | `education/pfp/python/tests/test_preflight_request_isolation.py::test_private_oracle_never_enters_request`; inspect recording-transport bytes and schema provenance. |
| 2 | RED if `3.9`, `true`, duplicate keys or an unknown checker are accepted. Keep strict parsing and registered dispatch rather than synthesize a reply. | Same file, `test_malformed_and_unregistered_replies_never_accept`; private finite integer oracle and actual status. |
| 3 | Transplant an observation to another request, then alter one response byte. Require digest/binding refusal with zero sends and unchanged originals; recover using the original bound bytes. | `education/pfp/python/tests/test_preflight_observation_custody.py::test_transplant_tamper_and_restore`; independent SHA-256 and send count. |
| 4 | RED a one-request shared adapter when missing billing metadata or timeout releases a reservation or retries. Implement only durable uncertainty retention and reconciliation. | `symbol_game/tests/integration/test_pfp_preflight_reservations.py::test_unknown_cost_keeps_reservation`; integer journal and recording transport, dependent on PFP-002. |

**Theoretical Minimum:** INVARIANT: the bounded behavior above. BREAK: the negative inputs in the ordered slices. WITNESS: actual returned value/refusal plus persisted bytes or send counts, compared with the stated independent oracle. MUTATION: Remove the request-digest comparison in [live_evaluator._load_observation](../../../../education/pilots/live_evaluator.py); the transplant test must fail. Remove duplicate-key rejection in [checker_registry.py](../../../../education/pfp/domain/pilots/checker_registry.py); the malformed test must fail. Source existence was checked for this plan; mutation execution and RED recovery are still prospective. Do not count a mock-only verdict or a skipped native test as verification.

**Proposed small-batch commands:** Run each named test first with `-k <test_name>` to demonstrate RED, implement the minimum GREEN, then run the one-file regression command below before refactoring. Paths labeled proposed are not claimed to exist. Commands are not execution receipts.

~~~powershell
py -3.12 -m pytest education/pfp/python/tests/test_preflight_request_isolation.py -q
py -3.12 -m pytest education/pfp/python/tests/test_preflight_observation_custody.py -q
py -3.12 -m pytest symbol_game/tests/integration/test_pfp_preflight_reservations.py -q
~~~

**Cross-epic sink ownership:** Education owns prompt/spec/checker and four-file source bundles; Providers owns admission/reservation/dispatch/settlement; Symbol Game owns the proposed durable pilot application and observation/evaluation journal. PFP-005 consumes reconciled paired evidence and cannot relabel PFP-000 regrading as efficacy evidence. Contracts/schema changes go to Governance; execution evidence stays outside epics. A producer supplies immutable source evidence; the consumer validates its own contract and emits its own scoped receipt. No downstream plan may reuse a producer PASS as an admission decision.

**Scope and evidence ceiling:** Historical audit counts are not current inventory. Ground-truth isolation does not validate every PFP-DEMO oracle, authorize a provider campaign or qualify efficacy. Shared-helper deduplication follows measured common behavior; independent judges stay separate. Record any eventual SoftwareQaReceiptV1 with exact command, runtime version, exit status, tested scope, base/head and source digests, failing input, mutation diff, and recovery output outside `plans/epics/`. This planning update executes none of these proposed tests and grants no runtime or admission authority.


Cross-epic ownership and retained custody follow the [integration decision](../../decisions/adr_20261010_epic_integration_ownership.md).
